<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lenin Boys</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lenin Boys were an armed terror detachment of the Hungarian Soviet Republic in 1919, led by József Cserny and associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibor-szamuely">Tibor Szamuely</a>. Travelling in an armoured train and in vehicles, they hunted down opponents of the regime and carried out summary executions, especially after peasant and counter-revolutionary revolts. They became the symbol of the Red Terror in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lenin-boys.jpg" alt="Lenin Boys" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_Party_of_Communists_in_Hungary.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
